<title>USA: QPQ says pact to buy Vitex ended.</title>
<headline>QPQ says pact to buy Vitex ended.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI BEACH, Fla. 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>QPQ Corp on Tuesday said its letter of intent to buy all outstanding stock of Corporacion Vitex S.A. de C.V. was terminated by mutual agreement of the parties.</p>
<p>Mitchell Rubinson, president of QPQ, said, &quot;We are disappointed that the acquisition did not come to fruition; however, the company is focusing its efforts on existing lines of business and further expansions thereof.&quot;</p>
<p>The deal was announced in January. Terms were not disclosed for Mexico's largest latex glove maker.</p>
</text>
